## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) **`AIFeedbackQueueTriage`** surface at parity with `web/src/components/ai/AIFeedbackQueueTriage.tsx`, following the structure of the closest existing surface (`AIAutoTripNameSuggestion`).

**Delivered** (10 files, `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AIFeedbackQueueTriage.*`):
- Web `AIFeatureCard` + `useAiStream` + `withAiFeature('feedback-queue-triage')` ported to a `FeedbackTriageModel` state-holder (P1/S8), pure SSE parser/reducer/projection (Adapter), live + in-memory seams, Helix-branded views, and per-phase bodies.
- **Propose-only parity**: "Suggest triage" POSTs `{feedback_id}` to the fixed `/ai/feedback/triage/draft`; it never calls `useUpdateFeedback` (documented — the operator's manual controls stay the sole write path).
- All states render (gated-off, loading, idle, thinking, advisory, error, stale, offline); i18n via the P1/S10 facade; VoiceOver labels on every interactive element; `view.opened` telemetry. Every symbol is `FeedbackTriage`-prefixed to stay module-collision-free.

**Verification — surface is fully green:**
- `swiftc -emit-module` (Swift 6, strict concurrency, iOS 18 SDK) → **0 errors**
- **65 unit tests pass at runtime** (`swift test`, 0 failures)
- whole-tree `swiftlint --strict` → **0 violations**; `swiftformat --lint` → **0/3554**; placeholder gate → **0**

